{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, with instrumental music</b> — The Gaon [Saadia] said: This psalm is David's, and it was given to one of the musicians to play it always, like לַנֵּצַח. Others said: That the מְנַצֵּחַ is the officer who is chief over the musicians, like וּמְנַצְּחִים עֲלֵיהֶם, and this is correct. And it opens with mem because לַמְנַצֵּחַ is on account of its being known." "<b>And the meaning of 'with instrumental music'</b> — that it has two melodies. Some say: a musical instrument is called נְגִינוֹת. And in my opinion: there were in Israel instrumental pieces and songs set to many melodies." "<b>And the meaning of 'with instrumental music'</b> — that it was the beginning of a song, and the melody was written together with this psalm, and likewise לַמַּעֲלוֹת and הַמַּעֲלוֹת and עַל עֲלָמוֹת and עַל אַיֶּלֶת הַשַּׁחַר and עַל יוֹנַת אֵלֶם וְעַל מָחֲלַת."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:21.564678344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}